[{"id":65635,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/GNS.20construction/near/65635\">#6</a> I have given <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/GNS%20construction\">GNS construction</a></em> an Idea-section and a bunch of references, amplifying also the generalization from <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^\\ast</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-algebras to general unital star-algebras.</p>\n<p>Also I renamed the section “From the nPOV” to “<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Gelfand-Naimark-Segal+construction#ForCStarCategories\">For C-star  categories</a>”, since the statement there is a horizontal categorification, but in itself does not offer any category-theoretic perspective on the construction. </p>\n<p>An actual nPOV is proposed in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Gelfand-Naimark-Segal+construction#Parzygnat16\">Parzygnat 16</a>, but besides adding this reference to the entry, I haven’t added any details on this yet.</p>","timestamp":1512338865,"subject":"GNS construction","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":65687,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/GNS.20construction/near/65687\">#7</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>An actual nPOV is proposed in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Gelfand-Naimark-Segal+construction#Parzygnat16\">Parzygnat 16</a>,</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>also <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Gelfand-Naimark-Segal+construction#Jacobs10\">Jacobs 10</a>  </p>\n<p>(which Alexander Schenkel tells me serves to make all the universal AQFT constructions in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/homotopical+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#BeniniSchenkelWoike17\">Benini-Schenkel-Woike 17</a>, surveyed in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/homotopical+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#Schenkel17b\">Schenkel 17b</a>, generalize to star-algebras)</p>","timestamp":1512835103,"subject":"GNS construction","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":65688,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/GNS.20construction/near/65688\">#8</a> That makes me think whether it is interesting to consider the generalisation of correspondences of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^\\ast</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-algebras (ie a kind of directional Hilbert bimodule) to more general <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ast</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4653em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∗</span></span></span></span>-algebras. There are versions of the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts%20theorem\">Eilenberg-Watts theorem</a> for representation categories of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^\\ast</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-algebras, but it’s not immediately straightforward, and even some the notions bifurcate, depending on analytic considerations. See for instance <a href=\"https://mathoverflow.net/a/287615/4177\">this answer to a recent MO question of mine</a>.</p>","timestamp":1512868279,"subject":"GNS construction","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":65689,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/GNS.20construction/near/65689\">#9</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts%20theorem\">Eilenberg-Watts theorem</a>.</p>","timestamp":1512878590,"subject":"GNS construction","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":65691,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/GNS.20construction/near/65691\">#10</a> Thanks, Todd.</p>","timestamp":1512887582,"subject":"GNS construction","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]}]